// "Exile the top card of your library." — bare top-card move to the exile zone
// ([CR#701.13]: to exile an object is to put it into the exile zone; exiling
// has no dedicated core verb — `Move(<what>, Exile)` IS the exile). The single
// top card is peeked and moved as the per-iteration anaphor `It`, mirroring
// `Draw.ron` (`Each(Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: 1)), Move(It, Hand))`).
//
// The impulse tail "You may play it this turn." is a SEPARATE sentence that
// needs play-from-exile permission (`engine-cast-from-zones`); this macro
// covers only the bare move, so an impulse card still stays in progress on its
// second sentence.
(
    name: "ExileTop",
    template: "exile the top card of your library",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    body: Each(
        binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: 1)),
        effect: Move(It, Exile),
    ),
)
